# Dystopia: oil, step 2 — refining. Generated by gen_oil_refining.py.

reagent-name-dystopia-gasoline = gasoline
reagent-desc-dystopia-gasoline = The light yellowish fraction, boiling from thirty degrees up. Sharp-smelling, it flares from a spark; the fumes are heavier than air and creep along the floor.
reagent-name-dystopia-kerosene = kerosene
reagent-desc-dystopia-kerosene = The middle fraction, almost clear and oily to the touch. Burns evenly and without soot if the wick is trimmed. Lamps and primus stoves run on it.
reagent-name-dystopia-diesel = diesel fuel
reagent-desc-dystopia-diesel = Amber solar oil. Heavier than kerosene and will not catch from a match, but under compression in a cylinder it burns just right.
reagent-name-dystopia-fuel-oil = fuel oil
reagent-desc-dystopia-fuel-oil = The black, thick residue from the bottom of the column. Barely flows in the cold. Boilers and furnaces burn it, and under vacuum it is distilled again into oil and tar.
reagent-name-dystopia-lubricating-oil = lubricating oil
reagent-desc-dystopia-lubricating-oil = A ropy brown oil from under vacuum. Bearings, gears and cylinders are greased with it. Spilled, it is very slippery.
reagent-name-dystopia-bitumen = tar
reagent-desc-dystopia-bitumen = A black resinous mass from the bottom of the vacuum still. Hot, it draws out in strings; cooled, it sets into a crust. Bitumen for asphalt, roofing and insulation is made of it.

